WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.235
-i don't know if you know this,

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.504
but we're in the middle
of a Céline-issance.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.671
-you should have let me know.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:07.807
I would have dressed
appropriately.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:11.644
-some magazine said that it's
the rebirth of Céline Dion.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.313
We're in a Céline-issance.
And I go, "I love that."

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:15.582
-it's kind of nice.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:20.352
Well, I feel like I'm being born
every morning.

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:22.589
-yeah. When you wake up.
Thank you.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.423
-every day.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.559
-i thought it maybe started
with your dress

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.195
from the met gala last year,
which I have to show.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.297
It broke the Internet.
-what?

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.431
Did I break the Internet?
-yes.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.133
-good. No I'm joking.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.069
[ Laughter ]
-look at this dress.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.804
Ooh, la, la.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.873
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.877
Look at that dress.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.244
Stunning.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.948
Is that what you just wear
normally around the house?

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.116
That's what I think.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.651
-I go to bed like this at night.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.753
-Absolutely. Yeah.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.555
I actually asked you
for something that you do wear

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:57.990
in the house
walking around the house.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.759
We asked your publicist.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.827
-They gave you a picture
without my permission?

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:03.562
That's nice.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.431
This is you around the home.
This is what you wear.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:09.402
There you go. That's Céline Dion
around the house.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.337
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.905
-Well, listen.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:15.274
-It's gorgeous.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:19.545
-Well, you know,
I got to keep myself safe,

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.748
especially when I do scrambled
eggs in the morning

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.982
for the kids, you know?

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:27.920
-So, you coat yourself
in an armor.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.890
Congrats on the residency
in Las Vegas --

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.092
The longest,
most successful residency

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.761
in the history of Las Vegas.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:40.332
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:41.501
That's amazing.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.203
-Thank you to all the fans
for coming.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:47.072
That's kind of a game changer,
kind of a life changer.

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:48.608
'Cause you're like, "Yeah,
I guess I just live here."

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.343
It's like 16 years or something?

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:55.448
-I've been there for...17 years
living in Vegas. Yeah.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.682
-Wow.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.117
-Yeah, I was supposed to
be there for three months.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.219
I don't know what happened.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.356
-That's what happens in Vegas.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.491
-And what happens in Vegas,
stays in Vegas.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.226
-No problem. I got you.

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:10.996
Céline, I always try to ask you
a good "Titanic" question

00:02:10.996 --> 00:02:13.432
every time you're here because
I know you probably love those.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:14.600
-You know that's a long time
ago, right?

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.302
-I know you love
those questions, yeah.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.171
No, but here's
what everyone is saying,

00:02:19.171 --> 00:02:22.675
and this is still being talked
about on the Internet,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.177
on the interwebs.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.879
They're saying at the end
of the movie,

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:29.681
if Rose just scooted over
a little bit,

00:02:29.681 --> 00:02:33.352
just a little bit
just over here,

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:36.756
she could have saved
Jack's life.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.925
Do you agree with this?

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.193
-Don't put me in trouble.

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.861
-No, come on!

00:02:42.861 --> 00:02:44.897
America needs to know!

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.398
-What If they want to do
a "Titanic" number two?

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:48.867
-No! No, you can't do a
"Titanic" number two!

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:50.636
-No It's true.
-No, you can't.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:53.172
-Listen, first of all --

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:57.343
First of all, if you look
closely to the picture,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:02.682
Rose is maybe dead
or totally frozen,

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.985
and she's not quite
all there, okay?

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:10.823
Second of all,
he doesn't need an invitation.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.526
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.398
Come on, baby!

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:22.735
Make yourself comfortable.
Jump in. You know?

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.670
-He could have pushed her over
a little bit.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.906
-And then who did not think
about this guy who is

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:30.876
in the middle
of the frozen ocean

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:34.981
and that maybe all his body is
so frozen that he didn't have

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.515
the strength to...

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:40.586
♪ Jump in for my love ♪

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:44.624
-You didn't think that he could
♪ jump ♪

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.125
♪ For her love ♪

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:49.729
-♪ Jump in feel the touch ♪

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.866
♪ Jump in the water,
my kiss is in the night ♪

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.502
♪ Jump for my love ♪

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.270
Yeah, okay.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.473
[Cheers and applause]

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.313
Come on. We love you.
A little more.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.581
You're the best.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:11.116
-You're so sweet.

00:04:11.116 --> 00:04:13.453
We get to be silly on the show,

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.954
but let's talk about
your new album.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.423
It is out today.
It is out right now.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.291
Download it.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:22.094
Go to Spotify.
Stream it.

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:26.532
It is called "Courage," and
it's a great album cover there.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.433
Why did you call it "Courage?"

00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:33.673
-I called it "Courage"
because the last three years,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.275
my family, myself, my kids,
my family,

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.377
went through tough times.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.646
A lot of people go
through tough times.

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:47.420
And I really wanted to,
after the passing of Rene,

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.222
wanted to --
This is actually the first --

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:56.228
My first album in English
without him physically,

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:59.431
but he is always,
always within me,

00:04:59.431 --> 00:05:05.571
and when this song came,
that was called "Courage,"

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:10.042
it represented all the album
because it was hard.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.543
It was difficult.

00:05:11.543 --> 00:05:14.747
And, also, it's a message that,

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:18.584
you know, courage is
such an important and big word

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.486
that all of us have courage.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:24.156
And all of us at one point
in our lives know that we want

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:30.095
to use it, but, eventually,
sometimes, we might need it.

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:34.434
And we need that in our lives
to be able to hold on to,

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:37.003
to be able to find
our inner strength

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:41.240
and be really saying that,
"You know what?

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.342
I'm a mother.
I got my children.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:45.845
I love to sing.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.881
It's great,
and it's going to be okay.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.384
And courage,
don't you dare fail me now."

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:52.952
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.421
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.523
-I Love that.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.097
You're doing the "Courage"
world tour right now,

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:07.833
and I heard this may be
a rumor, as well.

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:09.134
This is almost like another --

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:11.637
-Everything.
Oh, you're laughing. I see.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:12.972
-No, I just heard
a rumor that --

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:14.440
No, I don't have a picture,

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.410
but I heard that you have
been known to drive --

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.311
-I don't even want to look
behind the desk.

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.146
-No. No.
I don't have a photo.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:23.482
I heard you were maybe driving
your own tour bus.

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.217
-Oh, of course I do.

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:27.153
I don't normally drive
my own tour bus.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.521
I drive my people crazy, too.

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:30.189
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:34.727
But you do that, and I heard
that you don't have a cellphone.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.128
Is that true?

00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:37.964
-Well, driving and texting at
the same time --

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:42.735
-Oh, that's true.
-The kid is thinking.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:46.506
-But I heard that you're getting
into a laptop,

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.040
you're getting a cellphone,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.775
and I thought it would be kind
of fun if me and you

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:53.145
took your first selfie.
[ Audience "awws" ]

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:54.780
Would you like to?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.483
Do you know what a selfie is?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.685
-Why would I take a selfie?

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.187
-No, 'cause [imitating Dion]
you have to take a selfie.

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:03.723
[ Laughter ]
Everyone takes a selfie.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.724
-I can try.

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:09.461
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:11.463
All right, no problem.

00:07:11.463 --> 00:07:13.365
A selfie of us. I will
take care of you, I promise.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:15.801
Ready? Hold on.
-Where do I look?

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:19.071
Where do I look?! Because I
don't want to have crooked eyes.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.240
Where's the camera?!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:26.612
Where's the camera, Jimmy?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:30.449
All right, let me just show
everyone what we did.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.985
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:39.424
-You see? But where do you look?

00:07:39.424 --> 00:07:43.563
-It's perfect! It's perfect!
Céline Dion, everybody!

